{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Stand, and I will hear what YHWH will command you.</b> The interpretation of Rashi, of blessed memory, is: wait for me at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting and I will give you an answer — happy is one born of a woman who is thus assured. And it would seem that it would have been fitting to say 'what YHWH will speak to me,' but on account of his humility he did not say so. And the fact that he said ואשמעה with the added <i>heh</i> — it is possible that it alludes to the final <i>heh</i> in the Name, which is the voice spoken of concerning it (Exodus 15:26): ״אם שמוע תשמע בקול ה' אלהיך״ — if you will diligently hearken to the voice of YHWH your Elohim — that you do what is right in the eyes of HaShem; and so he said here, for through the <i>heh</i> it will be heard what YHWH will command. And Onkelos alludes to this, for he said מה דאתפקד מן קדם ה' — 'whatever is commanded from before HaShem' — he said this corresponding to the attainment of Israel." "<b>And that</b> this matter was hidden from him and was not reckoned to him as a punishment, unlike the way it was reckoned in the section of the daughters of Zelophehad, where it is written in the section of Pinchas (Numbers 27:5–6): ״ויקרב משה את משפטן לפני ה'״, and they said that the judgment of the daughters of Zelophehad was hidden from him because he took a crown for himself, as it is said (Deuteronomy 1:17): ״והדבר אשר יקשה מכם תקריבון אלי״ and so forth — the reason is that the inheritance of a daughter where there is no son is a matter dependent on reasoning (sekhel), that it is fitting to give her precedence over the other heirs of the father; and even those nations that have no Torah rule accordingly, deriving from their reasoning that those who issue from a person's thigh take precedence in inheriting him, whether son or daughter; and since this matter was hidden from him, they reckoned it to him as a punishment. But the judgment of the Pesach in deferring the impure from Nisan to Iyyar is a matter that requires received tradition (kabbalah) and is not dependent on reasoning, that we would substitute this month for that month; therefore they did not reckon it to him as a punishment. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, derived it from a gezerah shavah of קריבה קריבה — 'drawing near / drawing near.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:59.370722208Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}